# Practera Permission Model Reference

This rule provides context about the Practera platform's new RBAC permission model.
Relevant when working on features that involve role-based access, content visibility,
reviewer assignment, or user enrolment.

## How It Works

The permission model lives in `practera-graphql-api/src/auth/permissions.ts`.
All access control flows through `requirePermission(context, 'permission.name')`.

**Never add inline role checks** — use permission-based guards.

## Permission Catalog

```
content.view.own           — participant+
content.view.team          — mentor+
content.view.all           — coordinator+
assessment.submit          — participant+
assessment.review          — mentor+
assessment.review.assign   — coordinator+
team.view.members          — participant+
team.view.all              — coordinator+
enrolment.manage           — coordinator+
experience.author          — coordinator+ (create/edit milestones, activities, assessments)
experience.settings        — coordinator+ (experience config)
roles.manage               — admin only (NOT coordinator)
reports.view.team          — mentor+
reports.view.all           — coordinator+
```

## Superusers (bypass all checks)
`sysadmin`, `cs_admin`, `inst_admin`, `system`

## Custom Roles
Stored in `experience_roles` table. JWT carries `roleId`. Roles with `base_type=admin` pass all checks.

## Content Targeting
`target_roles` JSONB on assessments/activities/milestones replaces the old integer visibility bitmask.

## Reviewer Eligibility  
`reviewer_roles` JSONB on assessments enables multi-role reviewer pools.

